# Day 50

## Experiment Title

Creating Jenkins Pipelines for Automation


## Objective

To understand how Jenkins pipelines are created and used for workflow automation.


## Theory

Jenkins pipelines are a series of automated steps used to define Continuous Integration and deployment workflows. Pipelines help developers automate tasks such as building, testing, and deploying applications.

Jenkins pipelines can be written using a Jenkinsfile which contains the pipeline stages and execution instructions. Pipeline automation improves development speed and reduces manual configuration.


## Requirements

Jenkins

Java Development Kit

GitHub Repository

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Jenkins dashboard.

Create a new pipeline project in Jenkins.

Configure the pipeline settings and execution stages.

Create a Jenkinsfile for defining the pipeline workflow.

Save the pipeline configuration.

Execute the pipeline and observe the automation stages.


## Output

The Jenkins pipeline was created successfully.

Pipeline execution completed successfully through different stages.

Automation workflow details were displayed correctly in Jenkins.


## Result

Successfully created and executed Jenkins pipelines for automation.
